okf_version: "1.0"
request: Display received runtime errors in webchat while retaining independent app stream.
branch: nightly
implementation:
  - Web Chat subscribes to runtime.error on existing authenticated EventSource path after instance identity check.
  - Renders errors as system text bubbles; retrying flag shown; no markup execution.
  - Bounded ID deduplication; stops error stream if runtime identity changes.
  - Does not invoke sendMessage or POST to channel input; external event consumers unchanged.
verification:
  - Actual installed Chrome, headless Playwright, production rendered HTML and controlled SSE responses.
  - Duplicate error frames produced one bubble; outgoing POST count0; script markup remained literal text.
  - Screenshot inspected: C:/Users/djlov/AppData/Local/Temp/ciel-webchat-runtime-error.png
  - Browser2, runtime287 (19 skipped), architecture2 tests passed; targeted ruff passed.
limits:
  - UI bubbles are not stored in channel history; recent event retention remains bounded in-memory.
  - No remote deployment or push performed.
